fc8ea929278591fad0db871f59d75d9207475a5", "hash": "f322164cb0075467b13019afa86bca46ee1fbb6a5fb96ce3e91d179527ef92ac"}, {"seq": 519, "time": "2026-11-04T04:56:38.480825+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "collector", "content": "{\"url\": \"https://api.crossref.org/works?query=autonomous+goal+formation+intrinsic+motivation+objective+discovery&rows=4&select=DOI%2Ctitle%2Cabstract%2CURL%2Cpublished\", \"scope\": \"Crossref bibliographic metadata and abstracts where supplied; not full papers\", \"excerpt\": \"[{\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.20944/preprints202607.0905.v1\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Beyond Human-Designed Objectives: Autonomous Goal Generation in AI Through Intrinsic Motivation and Self-Directed Agency\\\"], \\\"abstract\\\": \\\"<jats:p>Current artificial intelligence systems remain fundamentally constrained by their dependence on human-designed objectives and reward functions, limiting their capacity for genuine autonomy and open-ended development. This paper proposes Autonomous Goal Generation Networks (AGGNs), a theoretical framework for architectures that synthesize, evaluate, and pursue their own objectives through intrinsic motivation. The framework specifies five components: Goal-Generative Networks (GGNs, based on a VAE-style sampler over a goal embedding space), Objective Evaluation Systems (OESs) with six explicit criteria, Intrinsic Motivation Engines (IMEs) implementing curiosity, competence, empowerment, autonomy, and aesthetic drives, Autonomous Agency Controllers (AACs) for concurrent-objective scheduling, and Self-Reflective Goal Refinement (SRGR) for closing the loop. We prove a goal-distribution convergence result (Theorem 1) under stationary feedback and a stability condition for the SRGR loop. The contribution of this paper is theoretical: we identify the structural and motivational ingredients an autonomously-goal-generating agent must possess. No empirical validation is reported. Section VI specifies the protocol — benchmarks (Minecraft-like exploration, creative reasoning, robotic skill acquisition, scientific discovery, multi-agent social tasks), baselines (curiosity-driven exploration, empowerment maximization, novelty search), and metrics (goal diversity, coherence, achievement rate, exploration efficiency) — against which AGGNs should be evaluated.</jats:p>\\\", \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.20944/preprints202607.0905.v1\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2026, 7, 14]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.1037/mot0000295.supp\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Supplemental Material for Autonomous Versus Controlled Goal Motivation Differentially Predicts Goal Progress and Well-Being Through Emotion Regulation Styles\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.1037/mot0000295.supp\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2023]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.5465/ambpp.2022.15984abstract\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Autonomous vs. Dependent Help and Creativity: The Role of Intrinsic Motivation and Goal Orientation\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.5465/ambpp.2022.15984abstract\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2022, 8]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.1017/9781316823279.017\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Reconceptualizing Intrinsic Motivation\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.1017/9781316823279.017\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2019, 2, 14]]}}]\", \"excerpt_truncated\": false, \"source_sha256\": \"9ca8f49701f26f8f7d056b9071d50b630fcb31f37a329a808fcdf62c4fd70985\", \"verification_required\": true, \"topic_domain\": \"unassigned_objectives\", \"evidence_role\": \"discovery\", \"host_tier\": \"discovery\", \"source_identity\": null, \"persistent_identifiers\": [\"doi:10.20944/preprints202607.0905.v1\", \"doi:10.1037/mot0000295.supp\", \"doi:10.5465/ambpp.2022.15984abstract\", \"doi:10.1017/9781316823279.017\"], \"source_candidates\": [\"https://doi.org/10.20944/preprints202607.0905.v1\", \"https://doi.org/10.1037/mot0000295.supp\", \"https://doi.org/10.5465/ambpp.2022.15